  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.3",
   "range": "LUK.9.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c6efe558",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.3#p1-c6efe558",
     "text": "But preach the gospel, and depend upon divine providence. Look you to your work, and God will take care for your wages. This the disciples might do, but this was no warrant to those maleferiati among us, who (if fame belie them not) pretending to an immediate call from God to go and preach the gospel in Galilee, sold their estates, set forward for that place, taking neither scrip nor scrap with them; resolving to trust God for their necessary sustentation. Is not this the efficacy of error? Are not these a diabolo dementatis, besotted by the devil?",
     "anchor": "Take nothing for your journey"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.4",
   "range": "LUK.9.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "89695b35",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.4#p1-89695b35",
     "text": "See Mat 10:14; Mar 6:11; Luk 10:11; Act 13:51.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 10:14",
       "ref": "MAT.10.14"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 6:11",
       "ref": "MRK.6.11"
      },
      {
       "text": "Luk 10:11",
       "ref": "LUK.10.11"
      },
      {
       "text": "Act 13:51",
       "ref": "ACT.13.51"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.6",
   "range": "LUK.9.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7fd2c650",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.6#p1-7fd2c650",
     "text": "Those miracles of healing ascribed to Vespasian by heathen historians (Dio et alii), but falsely, do belong properly and alone to Christ’s disciples.",
     "anchor": "And healing everywhere"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.7",
   "range": "LUK.9.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "17e275b7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.7#p1-17e275b7",
     "text": "Pendebat, animi dubius. He stood amused and amazed: he stuck in the mud, as it were, and could find no way out. This is the import of the Greek word διηπορει. Thus the wicked in the fulness of his sufficiency is in straits, as Zophar hath it, Job 15:22.",
     "anchor": "And he was perplexed",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Job 15:22",
       "ref": "JOB.15.22"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.8",
   "range": "LUK.9.8",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "630cf03c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.8#p1-630cf03c",
     "text": "See Mat 14:1-2.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 14:1-2",
       "ref": "MAT.14.1-2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.9",
   "range": "LUK.9.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fe5284c5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.9#p1-fe5284c5",
     "text": "With a faint and fruitless desire: for he never stirred out-of-doors to see Christ, though he believed that God had raised him from the dead. So true is that of Abraham, Luk 16:31. Perhaps he desired to see whether it were John or not.",
     "anchor": "And he desired to see him",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Luk 16:31",
       "ref": "LUK.16.31"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.10",
   "range": "LUK.9.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "16699906",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.10#p1-16699906",
     "text": "See Mat 14:13; Mar 6:30; Mar 6:32.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 14:13",
       "ref": "MAT.14.13"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 6:30",
       "ref": "MRK.6.30"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 6:32",
       "ref": "MRK.6.32"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.11",
   "range": "LUK.9.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "602bcdd0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.11#p1-602bcdd0",
     "text": "Weary though he were, yet never weary of well doing.",
     "anchor": "And he received them"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.12",
   "range": "LUK.9.12",
   "kind": "passage",
