   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "84a5e8dc",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.27#p1-84a5e8dc",
     "text": "See Mat 16:28; Mar 9:1.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 16:28",
       "ref": "MAT.16.28"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 9:1",
       "ref": "MRK.9.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.28",
   "range": "LUK.9.28",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7183896f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.28#p1-7183896f",
     "text": "Putting the two utmost days also into the reckoning. {See Trapp on \"Mat 17:1\"}",
     "anchor": "About eight days",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:1",
       "ref": "MAT.17.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.29",
   "range": "LUK.9.29",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7037d270",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.29#p1-7037d270",
     "text": "Dum ipsius mens tota Deo se immergeret, saith one (Luc. Burgens.). Christians, while they are praying, are often times carried out and beyond themselves. See Mat 17:2-3. {See Trapp on \"Mat 17:2\"} {See Trapp on \"Mat 17:3\"}",
     "anchor": "And as he prayed",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:2-3",
       "ref": "MAT.17.2-3"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:2",
       "ref": "MAT.17.2"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:3",
       "ref": "MAT.17.3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.30",
   "range": "LUK.9.30",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "30954b9c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.30#p1-30954b9c",
     "text": "Gr. of his exodus; in reference to that expedition or departure of Israel out of Egypt (την εξοδον). It signifieth a translating from a condition and state of hardship; and is also used by St Peter, 2Pe 1:15. Death to the saints is but an out going to heaven, Php 1:21, a loosing from the shore of life, and launching out into the main of immortality.",
     "anchor": "And spake of his decease",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Pe 1:15",
       "ref": "2PE.1.15"
      },
      {
       "text": "Php 1:21",
       "ref": "PHP.1.21"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.32",
   "range": "LUK.9.32",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e908b9fa",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.32#p1-e908b9fa",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Mat 17:5\"}",
     "anchor": "There came a cloud",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:5",
       "ref": "MAT.17.5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.35",
   "range": "LUK.9.35",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "574bc7ab",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.35#p1-574bc7ab",
     "text": "See Mat 17:14; Mar 9:17; &c.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 17:14",
       "ref": "MAT.17.14"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 9:17",
       "ref": "MRK.9.17"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.38",
   "range": "LUK.9.38",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "04998c55",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.38#p1-04998c55",
     "text": "As in the falling sickness, it happens.",
     "anchor": "And bruising him"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.40",
   "range": "LUK.9.40",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "35d92ed1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.40#p1-35d92ed1",
     "text": "Ponite, reponite, lay up (θεσθε) the sayings of my sufferings, notwithstanding this people’s vain applauses. The best balm cast into water sinks to the bottom; the baser sort floats on the top.",
     "anchor": "Let these sayings sink, &c."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.45",
   "range": "LUK.9.45",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "84805e43",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.45#p1-84805e43",
     "text": "So besotted they were with that carnal conceit of an earthly kingdom, still retained by the Jews to this day.",
     "anchor": "They understood not this saying"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.46",
   "range": "LUK.9.46",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "80e33dfa",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.46#p1-80e33dfa",
     "text": "See Mat 18:1; Mar 9:34.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 18:1",
       "ref": "MAT.18.1"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mar 9:34",
       "ref": "MRK.9.34"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.47",
   "range": "LUK.9.47",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6d02f845",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.47#p1-6d02f845",
     "text": "See Mar 9:38.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 9:38",
       "ref": "MRK.9.38"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.50",
   "range": "LUK.9.50",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "dfa8fffa",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.50#p1-a9d6d0a0",
     "text": "The word αναληψεως (Poly. Lyser.) implies a metaphor from fathers owning and acknowledging their children after long absence.",
     "anchor": "That he should be received up"
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.50#p2-1d28d86a",
     "text": "He steeled his forehead against all discouragements, εστηριξε.",
     "anchor": "He set his face"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.52",
   "range": "LUK.9.52",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f44d33d3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.52#p1-f44d33d3",
     "text": "Such is the hatred that idolaters bear against all God’s true worshippers. Illam domum in qua inventus fuerit haereticus diruendam decernimus: It was a decree of the Council of Toulouse against the Albigenses.",
     "anchor": "And they did not receive him"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.54",
   "range": "LUK.9.54",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a945681d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.54#p1-de5e831f",
     "text": "These two brethren, sons of thunder, how soon was their choler up! they had quick and hot spirits.",
     "anchor": "And when his disciples"
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.54#p2-e2633c97",
     "text": "It were to be wished that we would first consult with Christ in his word, ere we stir hand or foot to revenge.",
     "anchor": "Wilt thou that we command"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.55",
   "range": "LUK.9.55",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2a3b97a3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.55#p1-5b7fc010",
     "text": "He did it not slightly, and by-the-by, but seriously, and on set purpose; so must we rebuke and rebate our vindictive spirits, our unruly lusts, when like kine in a strait they rush and ride one upon the back of another.",
     "anchor": "But he turned and rebuked them"
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.55#p2-e1b016cd",
     "text": "Not of Elias’s spirit, as ye imagine; this wildfire was never kindled on God’s hearth, as his zeal was; you are men of another mould than Elias. He was a minister of indignation, you of consolation; his actions fit not you, because your persons are not like his. It is a rare thing to be of a heroic spirit, saith the moralist, Σπανιον το θειον ανδρα ειναι (Aristot.). Every man cannot be an Elias or a Phineas, Num 25:8. To that height of heat ordinary men’s tempers are not raised.",
     "anchor": "Ye know not what manner of spirits ye are of",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Num 25:8",
       "ref": "NUM.25.8"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
