  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.58",
   "range": "LUK.9.58",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c32c0d3c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.58#p1-c6262e7e",
     "text": "Christ had felt his pulse and found his temper, that he looked after outward things only; and therefore he lets him know what to trust unto.",
     "anchor": "And Jesus said unto them"
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/LUK.9.58#p2-dabb8bc2",
     "text": "Ezekiel with the Septuagint is, υιος ανθρωπου, the son of man, but Christ is ο υιος του ανθρωπου,, that is, the son of that man, of that first man Adam. He was the next and only other common person.",
     "anchor": "But the Son of man"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/LUK.9.59",
